Drop the ep_in_busy/ep_in_refusals reset from usb-bao1x's USB reset path.

usb-bao1x-serialrx-repair.patch carries this stanza, but it belongs to
bao1x-hal-usb-in-completion.patch: it resets the two CorigineWrapper fields
that patch adds. With the in-completion patch omitted -- which is the current
recommendation, see badge/README.md and task-8-report §34 -- those fields do
not exist and services/usb-bao1x does not compile without this removal.

Apply after usb-bao1x-serialrx-repair.patch, only in a build that omits
bao1x-hal-usb-in-completion.patch.

--- a/services/usb-bao1x/src/hw.rs
+++ b/services/usb-bao1x/src/hw.rs
@@ -343,23 +343,12 @@
             .map(|_| std::sync::Arc::new(core::sync::atomic::AtomicBool::new(false)))
             .collect::<Vec<_>>()
             .into_boxed_slice();
         for ready in self.wrapper.ep_out_ready.iter() {
             ready.store(false, Ordering::SeqCst);
         }
-        // --- local repair (not upstream) ---
-        // A reset abandons every queued transfer, so nothing is in flight and no
-        // completion event is coming for what was. See `CorigineWrapper::ep_in_busy`.
-        for busy in self.wrapper.ep_in_busy.iter() {
-            busy.store(false, Ordering::SeqCst);
-        }
-        for refusals in self.wrapper.ep_in_refusals.iter() {
-            refusals.store(0, Ordering::SeqCst);
-        }
-        // --- end local repair ---
-
         // re-enable IRQs
         self.irq_csr.wo(utra::irqarray1::EV_PENDING, 0xFFFF_FFFF);
         self.irq_csr.wo(utra::irqarray1::EV_ENABLE, CORIGINE_IRQ_MASK | SW_IRQ_MASK);
     }
 
